course: dictionary
lesson: 11021
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one is meant. Wave is a good example. «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air» means he is moving the book from side to side, so here wave is an action.
explain: «Waves cut caves into headlands» is a different meaning. Waves here are the moving ridges of water on the sea, because the sea is what cuts the rock. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put that meaning into the sentence in place of the word and check it still makes sense.
explain: «It sends the numbers by invisible radio waves» uses a science meaning. Radio waves are energy travelling through the air, so the word is about how energy moves, not about water or hands.
fact: Wave can be a noun (a thing: a wave, waves) or a verb (an action: to wave, waves, waved, waving).
fact: «Wave» can mean a moving ridge of water on the sea or a lake.
fact: «Wave» can mean a movement of your hand to say hello, goodbye or to get attention.
fact: In science, waves are how energy travels, like sound waves and light waves.
fact: «A heat wave» or «a wave of sadness» means a sudden rise of something; «wave» can also mean a curl in your hair.
exercise: «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air.» What does waves mean here? | *To move something from side to side | A ridge of water on the sea | A curl in your hair | A sound travelling through the air
exercise: «Waves cut caves into headlands.» What are the waves in this sentence? | A sudden rise of heat | Hand movements to say hello | *Moving ridges of water on the sea | Light travelling through space
exercise: «The heat wave made the whole town slow down.» What does wave mean here? | A curl in your hair | A moving ridge of water on the sea | *A sudden rise of heat | A hand movement to say goodbye
test: «Mangroves break the waves and hold the soil.» What does waves mean here? | *Moving ridges of water on the sea | A hand movement to say hello | A wave of sadness | Radio signals from a phone mast
test: «Wave your arm and shout if you need help in the water.» What does wave mean here? | To float on the water | *To move your arm from side to side | To swim fast | To dive under
exam: Which sentence uses wave as a noun? | They wave at the bus | We waved for a taxi | *She gave a wave from the bus | She will wave from the bus
